# Tests for the Eitc module (earned income credit, Form 1040 line 27)

Run with `clerk test`. Each named scope is one concrete return worked by hand
from IRC 32, Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.06 and the 2024 EIC Table of the Form 1040
instructions (`sources/forms-instructions/i1040gi--2024.pdf` pp 46 to 56), as
quoted in `catala/eitc.catala_en`. Every scope sets satisfiable inputs (a
return a filer could file) and asserts the expected credit and, where it
matters, the rejection of the wrong one. The whole printed table is checked
row by row in `test_eitc_table_golden.catala_en`; the oracle comparison is
`make difftest SCOPE=eitc`.

> Using Eitc as E
> Using Params_2024 as P
> Using Types
> Using Form_w2s as W

## Helper: a return with default answers

The default is a single filer aged 40, a citizen with a valid SSN, no
children, no combat pay, no other income than wages of $8,260 (so AGI is
$8,260), and nobody who could claim the filer as a qualifying child. A test
overrides only what it tests.

```catala
declaration scope Ret:
  context filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  context employer_income_subtotal content money
  context agi content money
  context tax_exempt_interest content money
  context interest_income content money
  context ordinary_dividends content money
  context capital_gains_or_losses content money
  context primary_filer_combat_pay content money
  context mfj_spouse_combat_pay content money
  context all_combat_pay content money
  context combat_pay_election_made condition
  context combat_pay_election content W.CombatPayElection
  context num_eitc_qualifying_children content integer
  context num_eitc_qualifying_children_for_calculation content integer
  context is_married condition
  context treat_as_mfs condition
  context special_rule_for_separated_spouses condition
  context treat_filers_as_dependents condition
  context is_mfj_dependent condition
  context filers_us_citizen_or_ra_all_year condition
  context filers_have_valid_ssns_for_eitc condition
  context primary_filer_age25_or_older_for_eitc condition
  context primary_filer_age64_or_younger_for_eitc condition
  context secondary_filer_age25_or_older_for_eitc condition
  context secondary_filer_age64_or_younger_for_eitc condition
  context eitc_qc_of_another condition
  context eitc_qc_of_another_required_to_file condition
  context eitc_qc_of_another_is_filing condition
  context eitc_qc_of_another_is_filing_refund_only condition
  context eitc_had_improper_claims condition
  context eitc_improper_claims_due_to_qc condition
  context eitc_improper_claim_taken_since_disallowal condition
  context eitc_received_improper_claims_notice content E.ImproperClaimsNotice
  context eitc_improper_claims_notice_expired condition
  e scope E.EarnedIncomeCredit
  output earned_income_credit content money
  output eitc_qualified condition
  output maybe_eligible_for_eitc condition
  output below_eitc_investment_income_limit condition
  output eitc_qc_test condition
  output eitc_notice_test condition
  output eitc8862_required condition
  output ko_claimed_spouse_combat_pay_without_mfj condition
  output unsupported condition
  output receiving_eitc_while_separated_checkbox condition
  output amount_without content money
  output amount_primary content money
  output amount_secondary content money
  output amount_both content money
  output recommendation content W.CombatPayElection

scope Ret:
  definition filing_status equals Single
  definition employer_income_subtotal equals $8,260
  definition agi equals $8,260
  definition tax_exempt_interest equals $0
  definition interest_income equals $0
  definition ordinary_dividends equals $0
  definition capital_gains_or_losses equals $0
